1 FILE /Users/suzja/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-Personal/Documents/FTM/Suzanne Tree Media/1864-FGW Ford-Shenandoah Campaign.jpg
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL fgw ford
2 _TEXT Cedar Creek After Action Report, Commander, 15th West Virginia Volunte
3 CONC ers, 3d Brigade, 1st Division, 8th Corps (OR, 43, 397-8)  HDQRS, THIR
3 CONC D BRIGADE, FIRST INFANTRY DIVISION,  ARMY OF WEST VIRGINIA, Cedar Cree
3 CONC k, Va., October 25,1864. LIEUTENANT: I have the honor to submit the fo
3 CONC llowing report of the Fifteenth Regiment West Virginia Infantry durin
3 CONC g the engagement of the 19th instant: Between the hours of 5 and 6 o'c
3 CONC lock in the morning of the action my command was in line of battle i
3 CONC n the breast-works in front of my camp, at which time the enemy were o
3 CONC bserved approaching in force within a few rods of our works. I gave th
3 CONC e order to fire, which was kept up until we were completely outflanke
3 CONC d by the enemy on our left. I here lost several enlisted men killed, w
3 CONC ounded, and captured. On falling back I reformed a portion of my comma
3 CONC nd in rear of the original dine of works of the Nineteenth Army Corps
3 CONC ; said corps giving way, my command was scattered somewhat, but afterw
3 CONC ard were collected in squads, and about 12 o'clock the larger part o
3 CONC f the command were reformed in line with other portions of the Third B
3 CONC rigade, the brigade being its line with Sixth and Nineteenth Army Corp
3 CONC s, from which position we moved to the left with the Army of West Virg
3 CONC inia as a reserve and support to a battery. About 5 p. m. we were orde
3 CONC red to advance, which was done in good order, but not without a loss i
3 CONC n wounded. The conduct of my only field officer, and a portion of th
3 CONC e line officers, I cannot commend very highly; but the conduct of som
3 CONC e of them is commendable, especially that of Captain Gandy, of Compan
3 CONC y E, Captain McCaskey, of Company C, Captain Porter and Lieutenant Laz
3 CONC ear, of Company K, and Lieutenant Powers, of Company B. The conduct o
3 CONC f the enlisted men who were present was highly commendable. The losse
3 CONC s in my command were as follows: 5 enlisted men killed, 1 commissione
3 CONC d officer and 11 enlisted men wounded, and 1 commissioned officer an
3 CONC d 11 enlisted men captured. I forgot to mention among the officers wh
3 CONC o performed their duty faithfully on that day was Lieut. F. G. W. Ford
3 CONC , Company F. The above report I submit. I am, yours, respectfully MILT
3 CONC ON WELLS
