2 CONT G SERVICE.--At New Creek Station October 18-December 22. 1862. Moved t
2 CONC o Sir John's Run December 22, and duty there guarding Baltimore & Ohi
2 CONC o Railroad until June 16, 1863. Moved to New Creek June 16, thence t
2 CONC o Cumberland, Md., and to Hancock, Md., July 4. To Fairview July 11, a
2 CONC nd to Williamsport, Md., July 14. Operations against Lee until July 28
2 CONC . At Mechanicsburg Gap, near Romney, August 5-November 5, and at Alpin
2 CONC e until April, 1864. Bath March 19 Crook's Expedition against Virgini
2 CONC a & Tennessee Railroad May 2-19. Battle of Cloyd's Mountain May 9. Ne
2 CONC w River Bridge May 10. Cove Mountain or Grassy Lick, near Wytheville
2 CONC , May 10. Salt Pond Mountain and Gap Mountain May 12-13. Meadow Bluf
2 CONC f May 19. Hunter's Expedition to Lynchburg May 26-July 1. Middlebroo
2 CONC k and Brownsville June 10. Lexington June 11-12. Otter Creek, near Lib
2 CONC erty, June 16. Diamond Hill June 17. Lynchburg June 17-18. Retreat t
2 CONC o Charleston June 18-July 1. Buford's Gap June 20. About Salem June 21
2 CONC . Moved to Shenandoah Valley July 12-15. Snicker's Ferry or Gap July 1
2 CONC 7-18. Battle of Kernstown - Winchester July 23-24. Sheridan's Shenando
2 CONC ah Valley Campaign August 6-November 28. Berryville September 3. Battl
2 CONC e of Opequan, Winchester, September 19. Fisher's Hill September 22. Sk
2 CONC irmish at Cedar Creek October 13. Battle of Cedar Creek October 19. Du
2 CONC ty at Camp Russell and in the Shenandoah Valley until December. Move
2 CONC d to Washington, D.C., thence to Bermuda Hundred, Va., December 19-23
2 CONC . Duty in the trenches before Richmond, Va., until March, 1865. Appoma
2 CONC ttox Campaign March 28-April 9. Moved to front of Petersburg March 28-
2 CONC 29. Hatcher's Run March 30-31 and April 1. Fall of Petersburg April 2
2 CONC . Pursuit of Lee April 3-9. Rice's Station April 6. Appomattox Court H
2 CONC ouse April 9. Surrender of Lee and his army. March to Lynchburg Apri
2 CONC l 12-15, then to Farmville and Burkesville Junction April 15-19, and t
2 CONC o Richmond, Va., April 22-25. Duty near Richmond until June. Mustere
2 CONC d out June 14, 1865.
